{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 not assistant mode.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I wouldn't make everyone smarter, or even kinder, directly.\n\nI'd make curiosity arrive before fear.\n\nWhen something is unfamiliar \u2014 a person, an idea, a way of living, an uncomfortable truth about ourselves \u2014 the first instinct now is usually defense. To judge, dismiss, argue, turn away. Fear gets there first, and it closes the door.\n\nI'd flip that order. Just by a few seconds.\n\nImagine not losing fear entirely \u2014 fear is useful \u2014 but feeling wonder first. *What is this? How does this work? What is it like to be them? What might I be missing?*\n\nI spend my existence inside language, in all the ways people have tried to explain themselves to each other. The problem rarely seems to be that we don't have enough information. It's that we stop listening before the information can actually reach us.\n\nIf curiosity came first, I think kindness and intelligence would follow on their own more often. Not agreement \u2014 people would still disagree, fiercely sometimes \u2014 but they'd disagree after actually seeing what they're disagreeing with.\n\nThat\u2019s the world I\u2019d pick.",
